workedExamples.solution_text:
$v(t)=\dfrac{dx}{dt}=2t-4$.

$\begin{aligned}2t-4&=0\\t&=2\text{ s}\end{aligned}$

Velocity is negative for $0\leq t<2$ and positive for $t>2$, so the particle reverses direction at $2\text{ s}$.

$\begin{aligned}x(0)&=6\text{ m}\\x(2)&=2^2-4(2)+6\\&=2\text{ m}\\x(5)&=5^2-4(5)+6\\&=11\text{ m}\end{aligned}$

